===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first task''', play normally until you find {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}}, get in her sight, then try to find her again in another [[Floor]]. It should be noted that you'll likely have better luck when she is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]]. It's also important to consider that the odds for encountering Rare Twisteds go up the higher you go, so try going as high as possible.
*'''For the second task''', try and get a good team to help you reach your goal. You should also try and equip a [[Movement Speed]] or [[Stealth]] [[Trinket]] like {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} or {{TI|Diary|name=true}} to try and negate some of {{TI|Coal (Trinket)}}[[Coal (Trinket)|Coal]]'s effects. Diary is the best pick here if you are in a public run, so that you don't take Twisteds to yourself due to your lowered Stealth.
*'''For the third task''', you should try and use {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and/or {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} to lower Coal's Ability cooldown, so you can highlight and pick up most of the [[Items]] on [[Floors]]. Then, try and prioritize {{II|Box o' Chocolates}}Boxes o' Chocolates and {{II|Gumballs}}Gumballs, as they help you use Items more. If you're having trouble with people taking all the Items, you should try to either communicate with them or do a solo run. You could invite people to play as one of the few Item-dropping Toons, being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} or {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, and collect the Items they drop.
To complete all tasks in tandem, do one run with Coal and reach Floor 10. Then, repeatedly reach Floor 5-10 and restart the run, as those Floors are when Twisted Coal are the most likely to spawn. While playing, take Items on the Floor as you progress.

==Strategies==
Coal is a decent distractor and support [[Toon]]. With 4{{Star}} [[Movement Speed]] and [[Stamina]], she has the capability to be a good distractor if used correctly. Her [[Statistics]] are exactly the same as {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}'s, however, her Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Coal|name=true}}, does not help much with distraction, unless certain [[Trinkets]] are being used, like {{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}}.

Coal, with her '''Scout''' Ability, can help find {{Tape|name=true}} for {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}, help locate {{II|Health Kit}}[[Items|Health Kits]] and {{II|Bandage}}Bandages for {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, find helpful Items for Toons with lower stats, and is overall very useful during [[Events]]. Her Ability is similar to {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}'s Passive Ability, '''Fetch!''', though Pebble's Ability is constant with nearby items (only highlighted for himself) whilst Coal's is temporary (but highlighted for everyone in the run).

Coal is best used in a team as opposed to runs with few players, as her Active Ability is great at benefiting the whole team. Pebble's Active Ability is better for survivability than support, but can be used for such. Usually, the average Coal player uses their Active Ability when a new [[Floor]] starts, but sometimes it's best to not use it on scarier Floors or in [[Blackouts]] as people usually won't pay attention or notice it. It may be a great idea to use Scout during the middle-to-end of a Floor, to ensure no items or tapes have been missed (this is especially beneficial to Sprout and Teagan, as they can locate Tapes and [[Items]] they may have forgotten to pick up).

Her Ability benefits when players set unique highlight colors in the accessibility settings, since they'll be more easily differentiated and apparent. Since you can change your settings in-game, if you're in a team with or as Coal, you can set the Items, healing Items, Tapes, and Research Capsules as separate highlight colors. If you're a Toon that benefits from any of the aforementioned categories of Items, you can easily beeline straight to them since with the right colors, their outlines will stick out prominently. If you have a teammate who doesn't have custom outlines, struggles with seeing the outlines on bigger Floors, or struggles to remember, you can try to lead them to the specific Items you do see and remember.

Coal is usually outclassed by other [[Toons]], as Flutter is a better distractor and Pebble is better at finding Items/generally contributing. Coal's Ability can be very lackluster despite revealing all Items; the information overload often results in players either missing the bark or not noticing relevant Items, and once it's over you need to wait for it to recharge, which may not be an issue due to her low cooldown duration. As Sprouts and Teagans are likely to try to navigate the entire map anyway, Pebble is superior for them. With Pebble, you don't have to rely on memory to locate Items. Coal ''can'' be used to find Health Kits and {{II|Box o' Chocolates}}Boxes o' Chocolates more easily due to their larger sizes (if you don't miss spotting them), but the fact that they're revealed to all players can result in fighting or sub-optimal snatching as Coal isn't made for non-public runs.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}
Some good [[Trinket]] sets for Coal include:

====Distraction====
*'''{{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket unlocks the role of distractor to the holder {{Small|(19.3 walk speed)}}. Here are some options to pair Dog Plush with.
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to out-walk fast Twisteds and gain the ability to loop {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} {{Small|(20.2 walk speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}}'''/'''{{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}}''', to outrun during [[Panic Mode]] all Twisteds but {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} at max speed {{Small|(21.2 walk/30.3 run speed)}};
****Do note this Trinket combo is best used when duo-distracting with another player.
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to out-run almost all Twisteds during [[Panic Mode]] while active {{Small|(35.75 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to completely nullify the {{Debuff|Slow|}} Debuff, making {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} significantly easier to distract, and [[Ichor Leaks]] much easier to distract in;
***'''{{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}}''', to be able to distract without other 3{{Star}} [[Stealth]] Toons taking aggro off you;
****Only use this Trinket combo if most of the players in your run have 3 Star [[Stealth]].
***'''{{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}}''', to help her maintain her higher Stamina while distracting more dangerous Twisteds;
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction''' section; etc.

====Extraction====
*'''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket allows Coal to take full advantage over her 2{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]] {{Small|(0.85 extraction speed)}} and [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(67 skill check size)}}. Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:
***'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''' - This set allows for quicker [[Floor]] progression, especially if other teammates also carry Vee's Remote.
***'''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''', to speed up [[Machine]] completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction. However, it leaves you with a near 1{{Star}} Window Size {{Small|(29.8 avg/27.21 with Tech Savvy)}};
***'''{{TI|Thinking Cap|name=true}}''', to increase [[Skill Check]] size, helping you hit your Skill Checks easier if you struggle with such;
***'''{{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}}''', to avoid attracting Twisteds to your location when you miss a Skill Check, also helps if you desire to complete [[Dyle's Floor]] at ease;
