==Trivia==
*Coal, {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, {{CI|Rudie|name=true}}, and her owner {{CI|Bobette|name=true}} are the first [[Holiday Toons]] to be added to the game.
*Coal is the first female [[Toon]] to not have eyelashes because the hypothetical combination of that and her eyes being 3D would not work properly.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1330898262395195442</ref>
*Coal's Active [[Ability]] ({{AI|Coal|name=true}}) is similar to {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}'s old Active Ability ({{AI|Old Pebble|name=true}}) with the difference being that [[Items]] are highlighted for everyone rather than just herself.
**Coal's Ability also used to have a cooldown of 100 seconds, but in the [[2025 Christmas Event]], the cooldown was reduced to 30 seconds.
***This is the largest decrease in Ability cooldown so far in the [[Game]]'s history.
*Coal's interaction with {{CI|Connie|name=true}} implies [[Bobette]] overfeeds her, and her interaction with {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} further adds to this, as Coal barks out of implied happiness when promised treats. It can also be implied she might be overweight, even if she were to be coded after a naturally large dog breed, and might be even more rotund than all the other confirmed chubby [[Toons]].
*Coal is the only [[Christmas Toon]] to not have been teased prior to the [[Christmas Event]].
**This makes her one of the few [[Toons]] that came out as a surprise, sharing this trait with {{CI|Finn|name=true}} or {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}, as they were not teased prior to their respective updates either.
*Coal is the second [[Toon]] (after [[Pebble]]) to have 3D eyes as opposed to the usual 2D eyes.
*When [[Bobette]] gossips about [[Pebble]], it's revealed him and Coal are friends. Their friendship is further emphasized with how one of Coal's [[Mastery]] quests include surviving 5 rounds with him. Coal and Pebble aren't related<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1327780196002037830</ref>.
*Coal is the first [[Toon]] to have a {{Type|Main}} Toon involved with one of their [[Mastery]] quests, with the second being {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}.
**However, Coal requires a specific Main Character Toon for her Mastery, [[Pebble]], while Gourdy requires any Main Character Toon.
*When [[Bobette]] interacts with [[Pebble]], she reveals Coal was tiny when first receiving her. How tiny specifically is unknown.
*Coal and [[Cocoa]] both had difficult transitions from 2D to 3D.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1366508342805139526</ref> Despite their small, simple shape, Coal's eyebrows took approximately 6 to 8 attempts to model.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1366508509012820069</ref>
*Coal's {{Skin|Pretty Present}} leg models are shorter than her Vintage and Default Skins', making her legs disconnect from her body when she runs.
*Coal's Active [[Ability]] highlights {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}} as a normal capsule. This stays true even when he is active, as the 'capsule' indicator clips through his lower body, and is intentional to further trick players into waking him up.
*Coal is the second [[Toon]] to have her [[Trinket]] be the same object as herself, with {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} being the first (though his {{TI|Magnifying Glass}}[[Magnifying Glass|Trinket]] is the same name as his humanoid).
*If you enter the Lore Room on the [[Seasonal Room]] as Coal, her dialogue reads "{{Text|(Whine whine)}}", making her the third [[Toon]] (along with all the other [[Christmas Toons]]) with dialogue outside of being in the [[Elevator]], using an [[Ability]] or finishing a [[Machine]], with {{CI|Vee|name=true}} being the first, and [[Gourdy]] being the second.
**Coal and the other 2 non-[[Main Character]] Christmas Toons are the first Toons to have these dialogues in a "Lore Room" that is not theirs (being [[Bobette|her owner]]'s instead). They are also the first non-[[Main Character]] Toons to have dialogues in a "Lore Room".
*All of the canine [[Toons]] (Coal, [[Pebble]], and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}) are implied to have staring problems according to various interactions.
*Coal shares some similarities with {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}.
**Both of their [[Twisted]] counterparts are {{Type|Rare}}.
**They are the first duo of [[Toons]] to share the exact same [[Statistics]].
**They and their respective duo members ([[Pebble]] and [[Flyte]]) are inspired by animals (Coal and [[Pebble]] are dog-coded and Flutter and Flyte are butterflies). The larger members of each duo are more laid-back than the smaller, much giddier ones, but despite their differences, they get along well and are patient with each other.
**They were both released with 3 other Toons, one for each rarity.
*Coal is the fifth [[Toon]] to have both themselves and their {{CI|Twisted Coal}}[[Twisted Coal|Twisted counterpart]] be in a thumbnail, being the [[Changelog|v0.6]] and v0.14 thumbnails.
*According to Bobette's [[gossip]] and Coal's interaction with [[Rudie]], she does not like the holiday she represents.
*Coal's cheeks and flag (only visible in her full render) were updated in [[Changelog|v0.14.1]], with the tips of the "snowflakes" changed to have points more faithful to snowflakes instead of hearts. This led her to getting a new full render in [[Changelog|v0.27.1]].
**This made her the first eligible [[Toon]], along with [[Bobette]], to have a chance to have her render updated, along with their [[Twisted]] counterparts, unless you count [[Rodger]] and his repose.
*Coal is the only {{Type|Rare}} [[Event Toon]] to completely be an animal, as compared to being anthropomorphic like [[Cocoa]] and [[Eclipse]].
*Coal, [[Ginger]], and [[Rudie]] are the sixth [[Toons]] to appear in 2 separate thumbnails, appearing in the [[Changelog|v0.14]] and v0.14.10 thumbnails.
*The snow in {{GoldenColor|Snowy Rescue Coal}} is in the same position as the dust in her {{GoldenColor|Golden Dust}} [[Skin]].
*Coal and [[Shrimpo]] are the only [[Toons]] that have never been seen smiling nor making any other face expressions at all, both in-game or in any official doodles.
*There was a bug that affected Coal, [[Pebble]], and [[Flutter]], where they would say [[Soulvester]]'s [[Ability]] dialogue while wearing his mask during the [[Haunted Gala]] [[Floor Event]]. Coal and Pebble shouldn't be able to talk English due to their dog-like behavior, so the bug was eventually fixed to prevent them from breaking character in [[Changelog|v0.29.5]].

